+# Preview expressions while changing a look
+
+Add one native Preview mood selector at the start of the existing Face options. Values are the current five moods, with visible labels Happy, Content, Tired, Scruffy and Unwell. The default is Happy. This is local preview state, outside the pet draft/save model; saved health, pet mood and worn clothing stay intact. The helper reads See how your look appears in each mood. The actual character image includes the selected expression in its accessible name. Eye/cheek option thumbnails retain their existing happy-face crops so each style remains recognizable.
+
+The existing CreatorPreview receives the selected mood and uses the same production sampler/renderer at rest. Changing mood cancels an active cheer before paint. Non-happy previews remain static while species, colour, eyes and cheeks change; returning to Happy alone does not replay a cheer, while the next eligible species/colour change can run its existing finite1800ms cheer. No extra animation owner, listener, timer, save field or queue. Live/system reduction and hidden-tab expiry retain the existing policy. Closing/reopening resets the selector; resizing and tab changes preserve it during this draft.
+
+Use the current responsive Face panel and native44px field target. Cramped layouts already have normal page scrolling; the preview must remain readable and selector/choices keyboard reachable at default and200% root text. Build meaningful red tests for all15species/mood combinations, cancellation and stale callbacks, unchanged saved patches, restoring Happy, hidden expiry, reduced motion, tab persistence and remount reset. Then verify real keyboard selection, layered art across allspecies/moods, saved tables and pendingframes in one offline native browser at a time. Inspect representative desktop/phone/enlarged-text art and controls before independent review. Stills do not certify human temporal comfort or physical devices.
+
+The broad continuing user authorization covers this bounded extension. The preceding CSS reflow was frozen while the new design/red-test paths were prepared, then independently approved and saved as89a99c0 before implementation changed its dependencies. Heavy jobs remain sequential/capped with2GiB reserve.
